      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence directly addresses this. The Abstract states Twitter data makes better predictions about the language inventory per country, and the Discussion explains why: Twitter has fewer missing languages (comparing against census ground truth), and the authors offer a hypothesis that Twitter better matches populations weighted by GDP (i.e., represents wealthier, more urban populations) while general web data aligns more with raw internet usage. This constitutes an explicit hypothesis/reason offered by the authors for the difference."
